	If you are playing on a multi-user workstation, and there are
some Nethack Newbies out there, go into the game as a wizard until you
have a polymorph wand.  Polymorph your pet into something terrible,
and stay alive until ~level 5, so you leave a bones level.  Let that
rothe kill you, and kick back to watch the other people play...

	"Hey, what the f**k is a nalfeshnee?  And why is it on level
6? Halp!"

Nyuk nyuk!  Oooh, I kill me.

Another thing I do in lost causes is drop my stuff.  If I am going to
be playing the next game, I like to leave the good stuff that I have
for when I come down again.  One question, tho' : If I name things
(i.e. a balsa wand named Fire(5)), does it stay named for the next
guy?  I don't think so, but that would be a good way to cheat - esp.
if you are playing on your own machine.  Name all your stuff as you
find out what it is, and throw it around the room when you hear the
wailing of the banshee, and your next character inherits the good
stuff, uncursed!

Oh well, you gotta dream...
